 high she  felt he was at the latter end of the  medium  level of responsibility so that i think  early on was an indication of where she  might end up with the sentence she also  also talked about  the um aggravating factors  involved in his stabbing of his  grandfather  his grandfather's vulnerability remember  he was virtually bedridden he'd just  suffered a stroke  the level of physical injuries that were  inflicted in that stabbing attack 21  stab wounds to his face  seven to his body  and then she assessed the mitigation the  plea for mercy from his own lawyer  he'd always accepted his guilt he had  shown remorse he tried to get help for  his mental health issues and at the end  of the day the judge said she felt that  the mitigating factors the things on his  side outweighed the aggravating factors  so again  an indication how she arrived at that  sentence of a minimum sentence of ten  years and eight months but she did make  the very key point of course that she  felt having heard everything that he was  a dangerous individual and she had to  impose a life sentence um because of his  continuing significant risk to the  public um his continuing interest in the  illegal pornography and  the ferocity of his  attack on on his grandfather  martin thank you well let's bring in  former barrister and legal affairs  journalist  catherine baxi now so catherine it was a  difficult watch at that sentencing but  why is it considered so important for  members of the public to be able to  witness a sentencing live from a  criminal call like this well as the  judge said there this was a very complex  sentencing exercise and she took 20  minutes roughly to explain  the facts of the case the horrendous  background to  the man's life and the background to the  killing  if  the public only see a snippet of a  report on the the news or in in the  newspapers  they may not fully understand the reason  behind her sentence so today  this move hopefully will enable the  public to und